kosha total-momentum

  -- Total momentum of a system of particles: P_total = sum(m_i * v_i)
  -- This is a conservation principle, not a single-step formula.
  --
  -- It cannot be derived from a single [mass, sankhya, val] + [velocity, sankhya, val].
  -- It requires a dvandva group (multi-entity collection) — Phase 4.
  --
  -- Conservation form: P_before = P_after  (closed system)
  -- Derivation form:   P_total = reduce particles 0 (fn acc p -> add acc (mul p.mass p.velocity))
  --
  -- NOT a mantra node. Registered as a kosha concept only.
  -- Will become a nyaya-step node when dvandva groups are implemented.

  "linear-motion-varga-vishesa"
  "momentum-swarupa samgraha-sthita"
  "niyama-sthita"

  shabda total-momentum / total-momentum-of-system

done
